WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.091 --> 00:00:15.954
During the time that Edward was away from the palace, what had happened to Tom?

2
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.336
Did he ever think about Edward, the real king?

3
00:00:20.797 --> 00:00:25.100
At first Tom did think about the young prince who had treated him so kindly.

4
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.803
But every day brought Tom a new and more exciting experience.

5
00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:38.089
His confidence increased until he no longer feared being discovered as an imposter.

6
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.853
So Edward gradually faded from Tom's mind.

7
00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:48.278
When the day of the coronation arrived, Tom was happy in his role and looking forward to being

8
00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:54.724
crowned. The day began with a grand parade through the city.

9
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.563
Wearing a splendid outfit, Tom waved to the crowd from a white horse.

10
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.645
"This is all for me!"

11
00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:06.026
he thought proudly.

12
00:01:06.046 --> 00:01:09.969
"A few weeks ago, I would have hated all the attention.

13
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.793
Today I didn't even mind that it took lots of servants three hours to dress me!"

14
00:01:18.575 --> 00:01:22.718
As Tom scanned the crowd, he suddenly spotted his best friend from Offal Street.

15
00:01:22.738 --> 00:01:28.694
"Oh, I wish I could wave and Julian would recognize me!"

16
00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.315
Tom thought wistfully.

17
00:01:30.335 --> 00:01:37.881
"Julian would be so surprised to learn that his old friend is about to be crowned king—for real!"

18
00:01:39.282 --> 00:01:44.265
However, Tom also knew that if Julian did recognize him, his reign might be over.

19
00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:48.808
"Good-bye, Julian," Tom said quietly without waving.

20
00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.792
Lord Hertford rode up beside Tom, interrupting his thoughts.

21
00:01:55.168 --> 00:01:59.210
"This is quite a day, Your Majesty," Lord Hertford said.

22
00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:06.053
"The weather is perfect, and your people are delighted to see you smiling and looking so well."

23
00:02:07.613 --> 00:02:10.915
Lord Hertford handed Tom a small leather pouch.

24
00:02:10.935 --> 00:02:14.276
"Here's some money for you to toss to the people."

25
00:02:16.237 --> 00:02:20.259
Tom reached into the pouch and threw some coins to the crowd.

26
00:02:23.816 --> 00:02:26.799
A loud cheer went up, and Tom happily waved.

27
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.364
He was just about to toss more coins, when he noticed a familiar woman staring at him.

28
00:02:33.384 --> 00:02:36.287
"Mother!" Tom thought.

29
00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:40.570
His hand flew up to his face, covering his eyes with the palm out.

30
00:02:42.212 --> 00:02:47.116
Recognizing the gesture that Tom had always made when startled, his mother ran toward him.

31
00:02:47.136 --> 00:02:50.619
"Oh, Tom, my dear son!"

32
00:02:51.119 --> 00:02:51.640
she cried.

33
00:02:52.808 --> 00:02:54.950
"I knew I'd find you if I kept looking!"

34
00:02:56.771 --> 00:02:58.972
Tom barely glanced at her as he rode on.

35
00:02:58.992 --> 00:03:01.694
"I don't know you, woman!"

36
00:03:04.396 --> 00:03:07.398
A guard grabbed Tom's mother and pushed her back into the crowd.

37
00:03:07.418 --> 00:03:10.160
"Get away from the king!"

38
00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:15.403
Tom's heart broke to see his mother treated like that, but what could he do?

39
00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:19.306
He turned in the saddle for one last glimpse of her.

40
00:03:20.627 --> 00:03:23.589
She seemed brokenhearted, and he was filled with shame.

41
00:03:26.111 --> 00:03:31.536
After exchanging clothes with Edward, Tom had thought about his mother and sister, Nancy, every day.

42
00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:37.221
But eventually he had forgotten about them, just as he had forgotten Edward.

43
00:03:37.241 --> 00:03:42.745
"What's the point of being king if I must pretend that I don't know my own mother?"

44
00:03:43.226 --> 00:03:43.906
Tom thought.

45
00:03:43.926 --> 00:03:47.289
"I wish I'd never gone inside the palace.

46
00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.932
I don't want to be king anymore!"

47
00:03:51.872 --> 00:03:55.134
The parade wound its way through the streets toward the cathedral.

48
00:03:56.274 --> 00:04:00.016
People cheered and applauded, but the king rode with his head bowed.

49
00:04:00.896 --> 00:04:04.157
He kept seeing his mother's face and how wounded she'd looked.

50
00:04:05.498 --> 00:04:07.279
"Money! Give us money!"

51
00:04:07.719 --> 00:04:08.659
someone called out.

52
00:04:08.679 --> 00:04:12.721
"Long live King Edward!"

53
00:04:13.302 --> 00:04:14.342
someone else cried.

54
00:04:15.603 --> 00:04:18.644
But those voices were drowned out by the ones in Tom's head.

55
00:04:19.776 --> 00:04:24.879
He kept hearing his mother calling his name, and then his own voice saying, "I don't know you,

56
00:04:25.019 --> 00:04:32.822
woman!" As Tom rode along, unsmiling and slumped in the saddle, people began to notice that something was

57
00:04:32.882 --> 00:04:38.445
wrong. "The king doesn't look so good," one woman said to another.

58
00:04:38.465 --> 00:04:43.748
"Maybe the rumors about his health are true," the second woman said.

59
00:04:46.496 --> 00:04:51.618
"Your Majesty, this is not the time for daydreaming," Lord Hertford said.

60
00:04:51.638 --> 00:04:57.499
"People see your unhappy face and take it as a bad omen for your reign.

61
00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.901
You must sit up straight and smile!

62
00:05:01.821 --> 00:05:03.301
Toss them some more coins."

63
00:05:04.402 --> 00:05:07.683
Tom did as he was told, tossing coins and smiling.

64
00:05:08.663 --> 00:05:11.804
But there was no longer any joy in his smile or his heart.

65
00:05:14.004 --> 00:05:18.467
Just before they reached the cathedral, Lord Hertford had to remind him of his duty.

66
00:05:18.487 --> 00:05:20.688
"Come on, sir!"

67
00:05:21.088 --> 00:05:22.469
Lord Hertford urged Tom.

68
00:05:22.489 --> 00:05:25.991
"You've let some dreadful pauper upset you.

69
00:05:26.951 --> 00:05:31.514
Forget about her and think about this: you're about to be crowned king!"

70
00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:37.697
"She isn't just some pauper," Tom said in a flat voice.

71
00:05:37.717 --> 00:05:40.059
"She's my mother!"

72
00:05:40.079 --> 00:05:41.599
"Oh no!"

73
00:05:43.516 --> 00:05:47.159
Lord Hertford was so shocked that he pulled his horse to the side of the road.

74
00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:51.302
"I'd hoped that the king was cured," he thought.

75
00:05:51.322 --> 00:05:56.305
"But instead his illness has obviously returned.

76
00:05:57.186 --> 00:05:59.487
What a terrible day for this to happen!"
